{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"francium-written-squid","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"# S5 — Bound writable container layers and alarm on exited-container debris\n\n## Plan\nBound writable container layer growth. Prefer a Docker/runtime-supported storage quota if it is compatible with the current overlay2/root filesystem; otherwise install a bounded periodic reaper for exited containers using Docker APIs (`docker container prune --filter until=...`) with safeguards for live services and rollback images. Do not directly delete `/var/lib/docker/overlay2` directories.\n\nAdd observability for writable/exited-container layer footprint and a dedicated CloudWatch alarm at/near the configured cap. The alarm must distinguish this generator from Docker build cache and generic overlay/image storage.\n\n## Grounding\n- Docker overlay2 docs describe container writable layers as `upperdir`/`diff` under `/var/lib/docker/overlay2` and warn Docker owns `/var/lib/docker`.\n- Docker CLI supports `docker container prune --filter until=...` for stopped containers.\n- Existing compose services use journald logging and named volumes for persistent state, so deleting stopped containers should not remove source-of-truth state when scoped correctly.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Writable container layer accumulation has an enforced bound or a documented runtime quota; stopped-container cleanup is bounded and safe.\n- [ ] Running containers, persistent named/bind volumes, and rollback images are not removed by the reaper.\n- [ ] Observability emits writable/exited-container layer usage/cap metrics and Terraform declares a dedicated alarm wired to SNS.\n- [ ] Runbook explains diagnosis/remediation and explicitly forbids manual overlay2 deletion.\n- [ ] Targeted tests cover prune command construction/safety, metric emission, and alarm wiring.\n- [ ] Portability criterion: solution uses Docker runtime APIs and local tests; no CI-provider-specific dependency is introduced.","id":"910b-2d43-4482-4c64","parent_id":"6202-e1c7-c57f-4897","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["infra","gerrit","disk-ceiling","containers"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"S5 — Bound writable container layers and alarm on exited-container debris"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788375027119321123,"uuid":"cc60d129-a0c0-4e5e-92e3-ef99241bfe44"}